//@ ignore
// KNOWN FAILURE: under -O, a function with more than 256 live registers has its
// print() calls deleted.
//
// Not run by the suite (`//@ ignore`) because it needs -O and a very wide
// function; the reproduction is tests/run-pass/knowledge_octonion_structure.sio,
// which passes WITHOUT -O and loses its own PASS/FAIL block WITH it:
//
//   ./mad --native-v2-compile tests/run-pass/knowledge_octonion_structure.sio -o /tmp/a.elf
//        -> PASS
//   ./mad --native-v2-compile tests/run-pass/knowledge_octonion_structure.sio -O -o /tmp/b.elf
//        -> prints stop after "composition err"; neither PASS nor FAIL appears
//
// Measured: that function is 7057 IR instructions and uses 7088 registers.
// self-hosted/ir/opt_cleanup.sio carries ~90 register-indexed [_; 256] arrays,
// so every peel analyses a PREFIX of the register file. A use through a high
// register is invisible, the definition looks dead, and the sweep deletes live
// code -- at rc=0.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, newly reachable. While IR_MAX_INSTRS was 4096 no function this
// wide could be compiled at all, so raising the cap to 16384 (#1649) is what
// exposed it. It is not caused by the arena.
//
// DO NOT "FIX" THIS BY REFUSING THE FUNCTION. Both refusals were tried and
// measured worse than the bug:
//
//   skip all of opt_cleanup_function_mfi   -> SIGSEGV (rc=139). The structural
//                                             peels, compact_nops above all, are
//                                             not optimisations codegen can
//                                             take or leave.
//   skip only the register-indexed peels   -> WRONG ANSWER. A 60-function
//                                             stress program returned 95 where
//                                             every other compiler returns 56.
//                                             The peels are a pipeline whose
//                                             later stages assume invariants the
//                                             earlier ones establish.
//
// The real fix is widening the 256-wide register state, and that is its own
// change.
//
// Refs #1649

fn main() -> i64 {
    // Placeholder. The live reproduction is knowledge_octonion_structure.sio;
    // a self-contained >256-register witness is worth writing when someone takes
    // the widening on.
    0
}
